---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Pinhitch — Case Study | Mayank Solan">
  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <!-- Back Navigation -->
    <header
      class="fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-40 border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--background)]/95 backdrop-blur-md"
    >
      <nav class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 lg:px-8">
        <a href="/" class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
          ← Back
        </a>
        <span class="text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">Pinhitch</span>
        <div></div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- Case Study Content -->
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-32 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <section class="mb-20">
        <div class="mb-8">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--terracotta)]">
            01 / Product
          </span>
          <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-6xl">Pinhitch</h1>
          <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
            A hyperlocal community platform where people pin problems at map locations, discover
            neighbors facing the same issues, and collaborate on solutions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {
            ["Astro", "React", "MapLibre GL", "Supabase", "PostGIS", "Tailwind CSS"].map((tech) => (
              <span class="rounded-full bg-[var(--sage-soft)] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-[var(--foreground)]">
                {tech}
              </span>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Problem -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The Problem</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
          <p>
            When problems arise in a neighborhood — broken streetlights, pothole on Main St, local
            flooding — people face them in isolation. You don't know if your neighbors share your
            frustration. Local government feedback channels are slow. Community groups scatter
            across multiple apps.
          </p>
          <p>
            What if discovery could be spatial and immediate? What if solidarity and collective
            action started with a pin on a map?
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The Solution -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The Solution</h2>

        <div class="space-y-12">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Pin Your Problem</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Users drop pins at map locations with a category (urgent, civic, community, personal),
              description, and optional anonymity. Personal problems can be fuzzified (randomized
              offset for privacy). The pin appears instantly on the map with its category color.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Discover Nearby Solidarity</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Open the map and see all active pins within your viewport. Each pin shows a badge
              reflecting the latest update status (in progress, has ETA, escalated, resolved). Tap a
              pin to open the detail panel and see the full thread of updates and comments.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Signal Solidarity with "Me Too"</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Anyone can tap "Me Too" to register that they share the problem. Me-too counts are
              displayed on each pin, and for civic/community problems, each me-too adds resolution
              time (preventing premature expiry of active issues). This transforms isolated
              complaints into visible collective action.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Post Updates, Confirm Fixes</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Problem creators and contributors post updates tagged as "in progress," "has ETA,"
              "escalated," or "resolved." For civic and community problems, resolution requires 3
              confirmations from different users (preventing false fixes). Resolved pins turn gray
              and shrink, signaling that the problem is handled.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold">Rich Features Built In</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              <li>
                <strong>Heat/Pin toggle:</strong> Visualize problem density as heatmaps or individual
                pins
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Place search:</strong> Nominatim-powered search with no API key required
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Geolocation:</strong> Continuous GPS updates center the map on your location
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Interests & communities:</strong> Join neighborhood groups, wave to members, share
                skills
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Direct messaging:</strong> Coordinate within interest groups
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>FixIt rallies:</strong> Organize community work parties with helpers and plans
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Technical Architecture -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Technical Architecture</h2>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Frontend: Astro + React Islands</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Astro serves a static shell with selective hydration. Interactive components (map,
              modals, realtime UI) are React islands with <code class="font-mono text-sm"
                >client:load</code
              > or <code class="font-mono text-sm">client:idle</code> directives, keeping static pages
              lean.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Map & Geo: MapLibre + PostGIS</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              MapLibre GL (open-source, no API key) renders the map with OpenFreeMap tiles. Backend
              uses PostGIS (<code class="font-mono text-sm">ST_DWithin</code> queries) to find problems
              within a radius, handling geo-fencing with high performance. Realtime subscriptions update
              the map when new problems are posted nearby.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Realtime State: Supabase + Postgres</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Supabase Realtime subscriptions listen for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on the <code
                class="font-mono text-sm">problems</code
              > table. Inserts trigger a full refetch; updates patch local state; deletes remove pins
              immediately. All visibility is controlled via RLS policies.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Storage: Cloudflare R2</h3>
            <p class="text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
              Zero egress fees make R2 ideal for serving media in a hyperlocal app. S3-compatible
              API, so uploads use standard presigned URLs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Key Metrics -->
      <section class="mb-16 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Category System & Expiry</h2>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-[var(--border)]">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead class="border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--sage-soft)]">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Category</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Color</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Expiry</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Me-Too Effect</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border)]">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Urgent</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Red</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">7 days (fixed)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">None</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Civic</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Blue</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">30 days (extendable)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">+4h 48m per me-too (capped 60d)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Community</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Green</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">30 days (extendable)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">+2h 24m per me-too (capped 60d)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Personal</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Amber</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">Never (user-controlled)</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3">None</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--muted)]">
          This system balances urgency (red problems are time-sensitive), collective action
          (civic/community problems grow longer as more people engage), and privacy (personal
          problems never expire unless the creator chooses).
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Lessons & Takeaways -->
      <section class="border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Lessons & Takeaways</h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--muted)]">
          <p>
            <strong>Geo as discoverability.</strong> Map-based apps feel magical when you discover that
            dozens of neighbors face your exact problem. The spatial element creates immediate empathy
            and social proof.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Realtime is essential.</strong> Supabase Realtime subscriptions make the map feel
            alive — new pins appear instantly, updates flow without refresh, and the UI stays synchronized.
            Optimistic updates prevent perceived lag.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Privacy by default, public by choice.</strong> The fuzzy location feature for personal
            problems respects privacy concerns. Anonymous posting removes social friction. This balance
            attracts both activists and lurkers.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Expiry + community confirmation prevent false solutions.</strong> Auto-expiring problems
            ensure stale threads don't clutter the map. Requiring 3 community confirmations to resolve
            civic problems prevents vandalism and ensures credibility.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <section class="mt-20 flex gap-4 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-16">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="rounded-full bg-[var(--foreground)] px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-transform hover:-translate-y-0.5"
        >
          ← Back to portfolio
        </a>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
